-          "spanish": "Esta relación profundamente desigual pero mutuamente necesaria definiría buena parte de la historia latinoamericana del siglo veinte.",
-          "english": "This deeply unequal but mutually necessary relationship would define much of twentieth-century Latin American history."
+          "spanish": "Algunos historiadores dijeron que la doctrina servía sobre todo a los intereses de Estados Unidos.",
+          "english": "Some historians said that the doctrine served above all the interests of the United States."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "With a verb instead of an adjective, the pattern shifts slightly to *tanto como* (as much as) -- *necesitaba... tanto como la región necesitaba*..., not *tan como* -- so watch whether you're comparing a quality or an amount/action."
+      "content": "Use *que* after the reporting verb and move the tense back. Do not use quotation marks unless you are sure of the exact words: *declaró que…* reports the meaning, not the wording."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-eeuu-02-mientras-tanto-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-eeuu-02-mientras-tanto-gr.json
