   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*De tal manera que* (in such a way that, to the point that) introduces the concrete result of an action or process -- useful for showing just how far something went, not just that it happened. It's followed by the indicative when describing an actual completed result. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the passive with *ser* + past participle from B1 Unit 18 (*La ley fue aprobada por el Parlamento*). The participle agrees with the subject, and *por* names who did the action. It is common in history, when the result matters more than the actor: who was overthrown, what was closed, what was elected."
