 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.guerrafria.02.con-tal-de-que",
-  "title": "Con tal de que + subjuntivo: una condición explícita",
+  "title": "Impersonal and passive se: treaties and organisations",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Con tal de que* (provided that, as long as) states an explicit condition attached to an offer or a tolerance -- exactly the shape of US Cold War policy, which backed reform and aid on the condition that a government stayed anti-communist. It always takes the subjunctive. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *se* for general or unknown actors from B1 Unit 6 (*Se busca una persona*, *se buscan personas*, *se trabaja mucho aquí*). The same pattern suits the history of treaties and organisations, where it matters what was done and not who did it."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Se with a past verb",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "a singular noun: *Se fundó la OEA.*",
+          "the verb is singular: the OAS was founded"
+        ],
+        [
+          "a plural noun: *Se firmaron varios acuerdos.*",
+          "the verb is plural: several agreements were signed"
+        ],
+        [
+          "no noun: *Se hablaba mucho de la seguridad.*",
+          "the verb stays singular: people talked a lot about security"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Kennedy lanzó la Alianza para el Progreso, con tal de que los países receptores emprendieran reformas moderadas capaces de reducir la desigualdad.",
-          "english": "Kennedy launched the Alliance for Progress, provided that recipient countries undertook moderate reforms capable of reducing inequality."
+          "spanish": "En 1947 se firmó el Tratado de Río.",
+          "english": "In 1947 the Rio Treaty was signed."
+        },
+        {
+          "spanish": "En 1948 se fundó en Bogotá la OEA.",
+          "english": "In 1948 the OAS was founded in Bogotá."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Estados Unidos estaba dispuesto a comprometer miles de millones de dólares, con tal de que los gobiernos aceptaran alinearse con el bloque occidental.",
-          "english": "The United States was willing to commit billions of dollars, provided that governments agreed to align with the Western bloc."
+          "spanish": "En los años cuarenta se firmaron varios acuerdos.",
+          "english": "In the 1940s several agreements were signed."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Algunos países implementaron reformas reales con tal de que continuara llegando la ayuda estadounidense.",
-          "english": "Some countries implemented real reforms so that American aid would keep coming."
+          "spanish": "En Chile se prohibió el Partido Comunista en 1948.",
+          "english": "In Chile the Communist Party was banned in 1948."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Washington estaba dispuesto a tolerar prácticamente cualquier cosa, con tal de que un gobierno se mantuviera firmemente alineado contra el comunismo.",
-          "english": "Washington was willing to tolerate practically anything, as long as a government stayed firmly aligned against communism."
+          "spanish": "Se hablaba mucho de la amenaza del comunismo.",
+          "english": "People talked a lot about the threat of communism."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Con tal de + infinitive (same subject) is the shorter alternative when the person setting the condition and the person meeting it are the same -- lo hizo con tal de conseguir la ayuda -- while *con tal de que* + subjunctive is for two different subjects, as in every example above."
+      "content": "The verb agrees with the noun that follows: *se firmó el tratado*, *se firmaron los tratados*. When there is no noun, use the singular (*se hablaba*). The *se* form leaves out who acted; if you want to name them, use an ordinary verb (*Estados Unidos firmó el tratado*)."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-guerrafria-03-no-cabe-duda-de-que-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-guerrafria-03-no-cabe-duda-de-que-gr.json
